{"title":"2007 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be two positive integers and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> a 'chessboard' with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> rows and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> columns. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> denote the maximum value of rooks placed on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> such that no two of them attack each other.\n</p><p>(a) Determine <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>(b) How many ways to place <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> rooks on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> such that no two of them attack each other?\n</p><p>[Note: In chess, a rook moves and attacks in a straight line, horizontally or vertically.]\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For the first part, note that once one rook is placed, other rocks can not be in the same row or same column as the other rooks.  Thus, the second rook can be in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/4/9d42de090a4ce87ba386a02de55516af64691404.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"39\" height=\"12\" /> of the rows and in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/4/f74d52f7378384fa067e7726071a01e3ee643edf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"38\" height=\"12\" /> of the columns, and the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/5/3657b37b69a5e1029f9182897c6b5dc7492cc1bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^\\text{th}$\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" /> rook can be in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/5/35532288b09ca9ebf5b593d27c5728f17dc92259.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r-n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"13\" /> of the rows and in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/d/0cd90488cd327ac026f7ee4e4d28f4e76a939fe4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s-n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"13\" /> of the columns.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/1/051789964dc63cfee006e53140a80cee3d6091b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r-(n-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"85\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/4/0849bcbd3bcea780a10c8945c3b7e72b3265d176.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s-(n-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"85\" height=\"18\" /> must be greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> for the rook to be on the board, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> can be at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, and since a rook must be on a row and a column, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> must be at most the minimum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />.  Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/d/89d1b5115a82279a41151ecdfec74edcadcc3b47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M = \\boxed{\\min (r,s) }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"124\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nBecause there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> rooks on the board, the rooks would take up every row or column (whichever one is fewer), so we would consider the number of ways a rook can be on a given row or column (whichever one is fewer).  For instance, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/d/cfd845e20d82278fe12a71b864d16a987da8a225.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s \\ge r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" />, the rook in the first row can be in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> columns, the one in second row can be in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/4/f74d52f7378384fa067e7726071a01e3ee643edf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"38\" height=\"12\" /> columns and so on until we reach run out of rows/have no more rooks that we can place. For example, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/4/5543dc5ddf76275e8ec8098746f437ac044fc3fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s = 5, r = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"17\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/4/2047ec72e87ed9fc87e076f56527ab95379d87d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\cdot 4 \\cdot 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" />. We are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/0/090f60908a6f13be52d902a462846a02ca53bb4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\cdot 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" /> shy of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/3/2933f407c21ceb3f3ec8370f43cd5b939250ffca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5!$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" />, and this is because we have two more columns than rows/rooks. Thus, the number of ways to place the rooks are: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/3/6c3a4ec6917f7cd3373ee7505bf850f13b2e995c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\boxed{\\frac{(max(r,s))!}{[max(r,s) - min(r,s)]!} = \\frac{(max(r,s))!}{[max(r,s) - M]!} = ^{max(r,s)}P_M}\\]\" width=\"463\" height=\"54\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Indonesia_MO\" title=\"2007 Indonesia MO\">2007 Indonesia MO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Indonesia_MO_Problems\" title=\"2007 Indonesia MO Problems\">Problems</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2007 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2007 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2007 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2007 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2007 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2007 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2007 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2007 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 8\">8</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2007 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Indonesia_MO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"Indonesia MO Problems and Solutions\"> All Indonesia MO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017213815\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.022 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.035 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 208/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1044/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 52/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5941/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.788      1 Template:Indonesia_MO_box\n100.00%    6.788      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:18265:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017213815 and revision id 259093. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}